</div><div class="BRDSX_page" style="text-align: left; margin: auto; line-height: initial; width: 468pt;"><a id="ny20063283x1_def14a_106-info_pg3"><!--Anchor--></a><p style="text-align: left; font-family: 'Times New Roman', Times, Serif; font-size: 8pt; font-variant: normal; font-weight: bold"><a href="#TOC">TABLE OF CONTENTS</a></p><div class="BRDSX_page-content"><div class="BRDSX_block-main" style="width: 468pt; margin-left: 0pt;"><div class="BRDSX_h2" style="color: #000000; font-family: 'Times New Roman', Times, serif; font-size: 10pt; font-weight: bold; margin-top: 6.75pt; margin-left: 0pt; text-align: left;"><a id="tIRCBD"><!--Anchor--></a>INFORMATION REGARDING COMMITTEES OF THE BOARD OF DIRECTORS </div><div class="BRDSX_fpara" style="color: #000000; font-family: 'Times New Roman', Times, serif; font-size: 10pt; margin-top: 6pt; margin-left: 0pt; text-align: left;">The Board has an Audit Committee, a Compensation Committee, and a Nominating and Corporate Governance Committee. Each of the committees has authority to engage legal counsel or other experts or consultants as it deems appropriate to carry out its responsibilities. The Board has determined that each member of its committees meets the applicable Nasdaq rules and regulations regarding independence and each member is free of any relationship that would impair his or her individual exercise of independent judgment with regard to Neuronetics. The following table provides committee membership for the Audit Committee, the Compensation Committee, and the Nominating and Corporate Governance Committee as of April&#160;9, 2026. </div><div class="BRDSX_fpara" style="color: #000000; font-family: 'Times New Roman', Times, serif; font-size: 10pt; margin-top: 8pt; margin-left: 0pt; text-align: left;"> </div><table cellpadding="0" class="BRDSX_fintab" style="width: 468pt; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto; border-spacing: 0px;"><tr class="BRDSX_boxspacer"><td style="height: 6pt; width: 276pt;"><div style="font-siz